& [Purpose]
  + define the smallest deterministic host-ready byte contract over published effect-free semantic inspection without authorizing an actual host or I/O effect

& [SJSProcessing]
  + delineation selects only outer request dispatch success-refusal shaping bounded machine bytes response sealing and exact replay
  + semantic refinement defines wire as an in-memory one-value request-response representation rather than a pipe socket process service or transport
  + constraint reapplication preserves every nested inspection bound fault receipt order lineage digest and non-authority unchanged
  + pruning removes stdin stdout framing filesystem network MCP LSP service lifecycle concurrency authentication provider model and runtime concerns
  + seven-fold exhaustion finds no smaller seam that fixes interoperable request refusal and replay behavior for a future adapter
  + data-driven design makes outer profile operation nested request status exact result bounded fault non-authority and response digest the complete data plane

& [Requirements]
  + [CSIW-001] replay the exact four-file published source snapshot at22778 bytes and preserve the protected live C state
  + [CSIW-002] implement one separate safe-Rust effect-free cantor_sop_inspect_wire library
  + [CSIW-003] define request profile cantor-sop-inspection-wire-request/0.1 and response profile cantor-sop-inspection-wire-response/0.1
  + [CSIW-004] accept exactly one outer request profile one fixed semantic_inspect operation and one published InspectionRequest
  + [CSIW-005] strictly parse one bounded JSON request value with unknown duplicate trailing malformed and excess-byte refusal
  + [CSIW-006] preserve the nested InspectionRequest value without translation defaulting normalization or hidden input
  + [CSIW-007] call only the published cantor_sop_inspect inspect API for semantic dispatch
  + [CSIW-008] return status succeeded with exactly one exact InspectionResult and no fault on nested success
  + [CSIW-009] return status refused with exactly one bounded WireFault and no result on outer or nested refusal
  + [CSIW-010] preserve a nested fault code exactly when it fits the wire code bound and otherwise use bounded internal_fault
  + [CSIW-011] bound every fault message to at most1024 UTF-8 bytes at a character boundary without copying request source content into new diagnostics
  + [CSIW-012] include the nested request digest only when it is exactly64 lowercase hexadecimal bytes and otherwise omit it
  + [CSIW-013] include fixed capability kernel.sop.semantic-inspect fixed operation explicit wire non-authority and one domain-separated response digest
  + [CSIW-014] require result-fault exclusivity profile capability operation status request-digest shape and response digest during response parsing and validation
  + [CSIW-015] bound wire request bytes to the nested request machine bound plus65536 bytes before JSON parsing
  + [CSIW-016] bound wire response bytes to the nested result machine bound plus65536 bytes during parse and before successful return
  + [CSIW-017] provide deterministic replay validation that recomputes and compares the exact complete response value
  + [CSIW-018] preserve ambiguity Unicode spans empty pages pagination lineage nested result digest and all nested semantic faults exactly
  + [CSIW-019] produce no partial success when outer parsing validation nested dispatch sealing or output bounds refuse
  + [CSIW-020] expose no stdio filesystem path database cache socket network service process thread clock random environment provider model operator update remote or mutation API
  + [CSIW-021] cover constructive success empty page pagination nested refusal and deterministic byte replay in debug and overflow-checked release
  + [CSIW-022] cover malformed duplicate unknown trailing oversized unsupported operation invalid nested digest status exclusivity response substitution and digest attacks
  + [CSIW-023] pass exact workspace debug release warnings-denied Clippy format dual-host source formation and independent evidence gates
  + [CSIW-024] attribute publish and immediately bookend only after completion signature direct remote equality and zero-effect replay

& [AcceptanceGates]
  + [CSIW-A01] one valid wire request deterministically returns the exact direct semantic inspection result inside one sealed success envelope
  + [CSIW-A02] every outer nested and response tamper independently refuses without partial success
  + [CSIW-A03] static absence proves caller-owned bytes and published pure APIs are the only data and execution plane
  + [CSIW-A04] focused and complete workspace evidence agree with zero failures and governed ignores only
  + [CSIW-A05] publication records exact implementation and immediate bookend commits without merge executable host or effect authority

& [Excluded]
  + stdin stdout newline framing files paths SQLite cache index network socket HTTP MCP LSP resident service authentication concurrency sessions provider model inference process exit installation update remote machine product effect and merge

& [Status]
  + formed_for_exact_bounded_implementation_only
